      <h2><span class="num">02</span>What it fixes, specifically</h2>
      <p>Most amateur golfers fight one of two timing problems. They release too early (the dreaded casting motion), or they hang on too long and block the face open. Both produce the same outcome: weak contact, lost distance, and a ball that never quite goes where you aimed it.</p>
      <p>ARC ONE cuts through the vocabulary. You don’t need to memorize what <em>lag</em> feels like or study frame-by-frame video. You just swing until the click shows up at the ball. Then you swing again and make it show up in the same place.</p>

      <div class="compare" aria-label="Swing outcomes before and after">
        <div class="col before">
          <span class="tag bad">Before</span>
          <h4>What early release costs you</h4>
          <ul class="bad">
            <li>Casting the club from the top of the downswing</li>
            <li>Weak impact, thin and fat contact</li>
            <li>Ball flight that drifts right (for right-handers)</li>
            <li>Lost carry with the driver</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="col after">
          <span class="tag good">After</span>
          <h4>What the click trains, session after session</h4>
          <ul class="good">
            <li>Holding lag through the bottom of the swing</li>
            <li>More compressed, consistent ball striking</li>
            <li>Straighter flight, tighter dispersion</li>
            <li>More solid strikes with the same effort</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>It’s worth saying the quiet part out loud: this isn’t new physics. Coaches have taught lag and release timing for a hundred years. What’s new is feeling it happen in your own hands without paying for a studio session.</p>

      <div class="cta-inline">
        <div class="label"><b>30% off</b> plus free shipping on $50+ orders.</div>
        <a href="{{ cta_url | escape }}" data-click-url="{{ cta_url | escape }}" data-gn-cta="mid" rel="sponsored noopener">{{ section.settings.cta_label }}</a>
      </div>

      <h2><span class="num">03</span>Five minutes a day, anywhere in the house</h2>
      <p>The routine is simple. Five minutes a day. No balls, no net, no new clubs, no tweaks to your setup. Just the trainer, in whatever corner of the house you have space — then five swings before you leave for the course.</p>

      <div class="stat-row">
        <div class="stat"><div class="stat-num">5</div><div class="stat-label">Minutes a day</div></div>
        <div class="stat"><div class="stat-num">0</div><div class="stat-label">Balls, apps or batteries</div></div>
        <div class="stat"><div class="stat-num">15.2"</div><div class="stat-label">Folded</div></div>
      </div>

      <p>Results vary from golfer to golfer. But the first real <em>click</em> at the ball is usually the moment something clicks in your head, too.</p>

      {%- if figure_src != blank -%}
        <figure>
          <img src="{{ figure_src }}" alt="{{ section.settings.figure_alt | escape }}" loading="lazy">
          <figcaption><span>{{ section.settings.figure_caption }}</span><span>{{ section.settings.figure_credit | default: 'Golfer Now' }}</span></figcaption>
        </figure>
      {%- endif -%}

      <h2><span class="num">04</span>What golfers say</h2>

      <div class="testi-wrap">
        <div class="testi-head">From our customers</div>
        <div class="testi-grid">
          <div class="testi">
            <span class="stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span>
            <p>Dropped four shots off my handicap in three weeks. Didn’t change anything else. Just started releasing when the click told me to.</p>
            <div class="who">Rob K. · Phoenix, AZ · 9 Hcp</div>
          </div>
          <div class="testi">
            <span class="stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span>
            <p>My ball striking went from embarrassing to the best it’s been in ten years. All from ten minutes a day in the garage.</p>
