      <h2><span class="num">05</span>Where it won’t help</h2>
      <p>It is not a simulator and it is not a coach. If you’ve never held a golf club before, take a lesson first. ARC ONE assumes you have some idea of what a swing looks like, and it works by sharpening what’s already there.</p>
      <p>Also: five minutes a day is a <em>floor</em>, not a ceiling. The more reps you give it, the faster the click starts showing up in the right place.</p>
      <p>The honest framing is this. A single lesson often costs more than the trainer, and the feeling fades within weeks. ARC ONE is a one-time purchase, and it gives you the same honest feedback on rep one as it does on rep ten thousand.</p>

